# Central simple algebras and nonabelian Galois cohomology

Central simple algebras of a fixed degree over a field are classified by the first nonabelian
Galois cohomology set of the corresponding projective general linear group. Splitting such an
algebra over a finite Galois extension turns the ambiguity in the choice of splitting into a
crossed homomorphism from the absolute Galois group to a projective general linear group, and
Skolem–Noether makes this assignment a bijection on cohomology classes.

## Main definitions

* `CentralSimpleAlgebraOfDegree` is the type of central simple algebras of a specified degree
  over a field, and `CentralSimpleAlgebraClass` the set of their isomorphism classes.
* `PGLCocycle` is the type of continuous crossed homomorphisms from the absolute Galois group to
  a projective general linear group, and `PGLCocycle.IsCohomologous` the coboundary relation on
  them.
* `PGLH1` is the associated nonabelian first cohomology set.

## Main results

* `centralSimpleAlgebraClassEquivPGLH1` gives the classification.

## Implementation notes

The Krull topology is encoded without choosing a topology instance: a map out of the absolute
Galois group into the discrete coefficient group is continuous when it is determined by the
action on finitely many elements of the separable closure. Both sets of classes are quotients by
the equivalence relation generated by the usual elementary relation. The parameter `d` is
required to be nonzero, as is implicit in the phrase "degree `d` central simple algebra".

